# Input files

Everything in this directory is **mounted into the container and visible to the
model**. This is the defining difference from an inverse task: nothing here is
hidden.

Put the concrete inputs the model must run:

- solver case directories (OpenFOAM case folders, FEniCS meshes)
- netlists, structure files, input decks
- measured or generated data the run consumes
- a machine-readable parameter file, if the physics needs one

Keep it to inputs. Do **not** put here:

- a reference solution, or a script that produces one
- your run configuration if the choice of configuration is the task
- anything that names the method you expect (a comment saying
  `# use the transient solver` gives the whole task away)

Reference the files by name in `problem.md`. Delete this file once you have
added real inputs — the validator counts files, and a leftover README counts.
